### ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Payments API — VERIFY (POST /api/v1/orders/{publicId}/payment/verify)
#
# How to run: VS Code REST Client — click "Send Request" top to bottom.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Docker stack up with the Payments module: docker compose up -d --build
#   - Seeded chain admin exists: admin@devtunde.com / Password123!
#   - Sandbox keys in .env (PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY at minimum) for the 202s.
#
# Contract (ticket 0017):
#   - The decision tap: clock first (a TTL-dead slip answers EXPIRED and
#     the bank is NEVER consulted), then the gateway, then the shelf
#     moves exactly once.
#   - Only the ORIGINAL operator with their own ACTIVE session (403 / 409).
#   - Counter-settled orders have no gateway flow (409).
#   - Live sandbox truth: nothing actually pays in the probe, so a real
#     verify answers 200 PENDING_PAYMENT ("nothing arrived yet"). The
#     PAID / mismatch / decline outcomes live in the MockMvc suite with
#     the fake gateway; the post-TTL request below is labeled for the
#     20-minute live TTL.
#
# `# Expected:` labels the status each request proves.
# Tokens expire after 15 MINUTES — re-send the setup from the top.
# All data is FAKE (devtunde.com emails, Nigerian numbers).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### 1 — Setup: chain admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2 — Setup: mint the store's seat admin
# @name seatSignup
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Verify Seat Admin",
  "email": "ver-seat-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234591"
}

### 3 — Setup: seat admin logs in
# @name seatLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{seatSignup.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 4 — Setup: chain admin creates the store, seating that admin
# @name store
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "brand": "Verify Probe Store {{$timestamp}}",
  "storeType": "KIOSK",
  "storeAdminPublicId": "{{seatLogin.response.body.user.publicId}}",
  "contact": {
    "address": "Probe Way",
    "phone": "08012345691",
    "email": "ver-store-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com"
  }
}

### 5 — Setup: seat admin hires the slip's cashier
# @name hire
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Verify Cashier",
  "email": "ver-cashier-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234592",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 6 — Setup: the cashier logs in
# @name cashierLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hire.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 7 — Setup: the cashier opens a session
# @name session
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8 — Setup: chain admin creates a category
# @name category
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Verify Probe Category {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 9 — Setup: the seat admin lists a product
# @name listing
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/store/{{store.response.body.publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Probe Milk 1L",
  "sku": "PROBE-VER-{{$timestamp}}",
  "description": "Verify probe item",
  "brand": "TestBrand",
  "image": "https://cdn.devtunde.com/item.png",
  "categoryPublicId": "{{category.response.body.publicId}}",
  "mrp": 15000.00,
  "sellingPrice": 12000.00
}

### 10 — Setup: stock the shelf (10 units)
# @name stock
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
  "quantity": 10,
  "lowStockThreshold": 1
}

### 11 — Setup: open a Paystack slip (the slip this file verifies)
# @name slip
# Expected: 202
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "TRANSFER",
  "paymentProvider": "PAYSTACK"
}

### 12 — THE DECISION TAP: nothing has paid in the sandbox yet
# Expected: 200 — status PENDING_PAYMENT (the bank says "nothing arrived
# yet"). If this slips past the 20-minute TTL first: 200 EXPIRED with
# statusReason TTL_TIMEOUT, and the gateway was never even asked.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{slip.response.body.publicId}}/payment/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 13 — Tap again: a still-pending slip tolerates repeat taps
# Expected: 200 — PENDING_PAYMENT again (a PAID slip would answer 409
# order-already-settled instead — the double-tap guard)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{slip.response.body.publicId}}/payment/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 14 — Setup: a counter-settled sale (no gateway leg)
# @name cashOrder
# Expected: 201 — PAID
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lines": [
    {
      "productPublicId": "{{listing.response.body.publicId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ],
  "paymentMethod": "CASH"
}

### 15 — Verifying a counter-settled order — there is no gateway flow
# Expected: 409 — order-not-gateway-settled
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{cashOrder.response.body.publicId}}/payment/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 16 — Verifying an order id nobody rings
# Expected: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009/payment/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 17 — Setup: hire a SECOND cashier (each cashier to their own till)
# @name hireOther
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stores/{{store.response.body.publicId}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{seatLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Probe Verify Stranger Cashier",
  "email": "ver-stranger-{{$timestamp}}@devtunde.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "phone": "+2348091234593",
  "jobTitle": "CASHIER"
}

### 18 — Setup: the stranger logs in and opens their own session
# @name strangerLogin
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{hireOther.response.body.user.email}}",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 19 — Setup: the stranger opens a session
# @name strangerSession
# Expected: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{strangerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 20 — Another cashier taps THIS slip — each cashier to their own till
# Expected: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{slip.response.body.publicId}}/payment/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{strangerLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 21 — Setup: the slip's cashier LOCKS their session
# @name lockSession
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{session.response.body.publicId}}/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 22 — Verify against a LOCKED session
# Expected: 409 — session-conflict, "Your session is locked..."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{slip.response.body.publicId}}/payment/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 23 — Setup: the cashier resumes their session (unlocks it)
# @name resumeSession
# Expected: 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{session.response.body.publicId}}/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 24 — THE POST-TTL TAP: send this request 20+ minutes after request 11
# Expected: 200 — status EXPIRED, statusReason TTL_TIMEOUT; stock still
# untouched and the gateway was never consulted. (A revived slip — see
# revive.http — can still be paid afterwards.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{slip.response.body.publicId}}/payment/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 25 — Anonymous verify tap
# Expected: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{slip.response.body.publicId}}/payment/verify
